            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A typical syndrome of wandering testicular pain and unilateral hydrocele has been observed in three patients.. It is caused by intravaginal, which seem to arise from testicular and epididymal appendices undergoing gradual necrosis and subsequent calcification during torsion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
